; A match whose constructor arms name every constructor, but whose
; SUB-patterns leave a shape uncovered. Exhaustiveness collected each
; arm's head constructor and subtracted that set from the type's
; declaration list, so it never looked past the head:
; `(Cons h (Cons h2 t))` counted as covering `Cons` entirely, both
; arms together looked total, and this checked OK. At run time a
; one-element list matched neither arm, fell through to the merge
; block, and the match answered its freshly allocated result cell's
; contents - 0, at exit 0, indistinguishable from a real answer. At a
; reference field type the same hole answers a null handle, so the
; next field read segfaults rather than lying quietly.
;
; This is MM-VAL-9b's fall-through reached through a CONSTRUCTOR arm
; instead of a literal one, which 476 pins. Exhaustiveness is now
; Maranget's usefulness check over a pattern matrix, so the witness is
; the constructor missing at the hole - `Nil` in the tail column, not
; `Cons` at the head - and a nested arm that IS total still checks
; (tests/selfhost/740-nested-nullary-pattern.ax and 620, 810,
; tests/stdlib/120 and 270 are all that shape).
;
; `deep` is the same hole two levels down, which is what pins that
; the check RECURSES rather than special-casing one level: `Nil` and
; `Cons` are both covered at the head, the tail column covers both
; again, and it is the tail's tail that no arm leaves total. Note
; `(Nil)` is written parenthesised throughout - a bare `Nil` is a
; BINDER that matches anything, and an arm ending in one is total.
(data List (a)
  (Nil)
  (Cons a (List a)))

(:: firstTwo (-> (List Int) Int))
(fn (firstTwo l)
  (match l
    ((Nil) 0)
    ((Cons h (Cons h2 t)) (+ h h2))))

(:: deep (-> (List Int) Int))
(fn (deep l)
  (match l
    ((Nil) 0)
    ((Cons h (Nil)) h)
    ((Cons h (Cons h2 (Cons h3 t))) h3)))

; The CROSS-COLUMN case, and the reason the check is the real
; algorithm rather than a per-column merge. Each column of `pair`
; holds both `R` and `G`, so a check that asked "is every constructor
; present in this column?" one column at a time would call it total -
; and `(Mk (R) (R))` would fall through. Specialization asks the
; question per COMBINATION, so it refuses this and accepts the
; four-arm version (tests/selfhost/745-nested-pattern-total.ax).
(data C (R) (G))
(data P (Mk C C))

(:: pair (-> P Int))
(fn (pair p)
  (match p
    ((Mk (R) (G)) 1)
    ((Mk (G) (R)) 2)))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main) 0)
